 "sections": [
  {
   "h": "1. Executive Summary",
   "p": [
    "CodeSprint 2027 is a 48-hour national hackathon bringing together 300 student builders to solve real-world problems across three tracks.",
    "The event runs over a weekend at the main campus, with online participation for remote teams. Each team of three to five members chooses a track, receives mentoring from industry practitioners, and presents a working prototype to a judging panel. Outcomes include open-source repositories, internship conversations with sponsors, and a public showcase that raises the institution's profile among employers and applicants alike."
   ]
  },
  {
   "h": "2. Objectives",
   "bullets": [
    "Deliver hands-on, team-based learning",
    "Connect talent with industry mentors",
    "Publish 20+ open-source prototypes"
   ],
   "p": [
    "Objectives are deliberately measurable so that the committee and sponsors can judge success within two weeks of the event, using the metrics below."
